course: dictionary
lesson: 15626
title: Teething: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look simple but have more than one meaning. Use the words around them to find out which meaning fits. «Baby Mia is teething, so she is grumpy and dribbles all day.» Mia is a baby, grumpy and dribbling are clues, so teething must be the time when her first teeth push through her gums.
explain: The clues also tell you how it feels. «Mum gave Mia a teething ring to chew.» A teething ring is something a baby chews to ease sore gums, so teething can hurt a little.
explain: Teething has a second meaning in everyday talk. «The new school app had teething problems in its first week.» Here teething problems are small troubles at the start of something new, and they get fixed over time. Ask yourself: does the first meaning fit, or does the second?
explain: Watch the spelling. Teethe is a verb, as in «Babies teethe at different ages.» Teeth is a noun meaning more than one tooth. Teething is the -ing form of teethe, and it can also be used as an adjective, as in «teething problems».
fact: Teething means the time when a baby's first teeth are growing through the gums.
fact: Teething can make a baby grumpy, dribbly and keen to chew things.
fact: «Teething problems» means small problems at the start of something new.
fact: «Teethe» is a verb, and «teeth» is a noun meaning more than one tooth.
fact: A teething ring is something a baby chews to feel better.
exercise: «The baby was grumpy and dribbling because she was teething.» What does teething mean here? | A sweet drink for babies | Losing all your teeth at once | The time when a baby learns to walk | *The time when a baby's first teeth push through the gums
exercise: «The new app had teething problems in its first week, but they were fixed quickly.» What are teething problems? | Big problems that never get fixed | Problems with the weather | *Small problems at the start of something new | Problems with your teeth at the dentist
exercise: Which word fits the gap? «Most babies start to ___ when they are about six months old.» | tooth | teething | *teethe | teeth
test: «Mia had sore gums, so Mum gave her a teething ring.» What is a teething ring for? | *To help a baby feel better while her first teeth come through | To be a toy for older children | To measure how tall a baby is | To brush the gums with toothpaste
test: Which word is a noun meaning more than one tooth? | teethes | teethe | teething | *teeth
exam: Jayden says, «The new game had teething problems.» What does he mean? | *The game had small problems at the start that were being fixed | The game was finished and perfect from the start | The game is only for babies | The game was made from real teeth
